  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Bull Demon attacks while Heavenly Court’s Gu Immortal Cong Yan defends. He cultivates rule path. Countless blue lines on his skin resemble tattoos, thin or thick, some crisscrossing into a web that protects him tightly as each hit makes his body vibrate. Yuan Qiong Du, still refining Gu, judges that Longevity Heaven’s close combat is holding back to avoid wrecking the refinement path formation.",
      "chapters": [
        1717
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bull_demon",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_yuan_qiong_du",
        "fac_longevity_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Countless blue lines mark his skin like tattoos, thin or thick, some crisscrossing into a web that protects him.",
      "chapters": [
        1717
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His battle with Bull Demon stays even while both sides favor defense inside the refinement path formation. When Flower Lady enters Heaven Overseeing Tower, he and Che Wei try to retreat into the tower and are restrained by Bull Demon and Five Elements Grandmaster.",
      "chapters": [
        1720
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "flower-lady-diversion",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_flower_lady",
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower",
        "char_che_wei",
        "char_five_elements_grandmaster"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Yong names Cong Yan with Duke Long, Fairy Zi Wei, Yuan Qiong Du, and Che Wei as fighting in Heavenly Court while Southern Border weighs the nine-nine consecutive unceasing formation.",
      "chapters": [
        1730
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-among-heavenly-court-fighters",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_yong",
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration calls him Heavenly Court rank eight rule path Gu Immortal Cong Yan. He takes out rule path Immortal Gu Permanence, a splendid golden centipede-like Gu, and carefully sends it into the incomplete Eternal Yacht Immortal Gu House as the final construction step. The house goes out of control and shatters; he protects Permanence Gu at the cost of heavy injuries while supplementary Immortal Gu are damaged. Duke Long later tells Fairy Zi Wei not to blame Cong Yan for the difficulty of building an Immortal Gu House.",
      "chapters": [
        1795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "permanence-and-eternal-yacht",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "house_eternal_yacht",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "gu_permanence_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the refinement path Gu formation that feeds success dao marks to Yuan Qiong Du’s fate Gu repair, Cong Yan and Che Wei defend with full strength and sigh at Fairy Zi Wei’s dependability when starlight teleports approaching Northern Plains Gu Immortals away.",
      "chapters": [
        1937
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-gu-formation-defense",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_formation",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Heaven Overseeing Tower’s quiet top floor he laughs weakly that Yuan Qiong Du has finished and it is their turn. Che Wei says they can barely transmit voices, let alone activate the tower. Cong Yan answers that his remaining immortal essence can activate his trump card. Che Wei, a close friend, begs him not to absorb the injuries or he will die at once. Cong Yan speaks of looking forward to Che Wei creating a path, then spreads light blue radiance that covers Che Wei. Che Wei’s body recovers while Cong Yan’s worsens; Cong Yan dies, and Che Wei crawls toward fate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1952
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "injury-transfer-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
